Chapter: CheckErrorsScript

  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe
  cites Shell chapter ShellTypes
  cites Shell chapter ShellBuild
  cites Shell chapter Pipeline
  cites Shell chapter PowerShellEmit

 We say:

 THE NINETEENTH GENERATOR ON THE PIPELINE MODEL (PipelineModel.md). The emitted
 script is byte-identical to the one that shipped before the migration.

 EVERY STATEMENT HERE IS RAW, so `pipe-ref` binds nothing and no artifact
 declares a production: the three stages below are named, their inputs and
 resources are declared, and their FOUR refusals are written down, which is all
 the model can reach into a script spelled this way. The verdicts are the
 return on the migration, because all four exits are inside raw payloads and
 no walk of the bodies would find any of them.

 THIS SCRIPT'S `-Jobs` IS REAL, unlike `sweep-apps`': it reaches
 `ForEach-Object -ThrottleLimit`, so the stage below declares a parallelism the
 caller actually controls.

Section: Parameters

 -Kernel carries the doc block because the default is the trap: compile.ps1
 falls back to build-output/bare-metal/Codex.cdx, which holds whichever
 kernel ran LAST, so a check that omits it can judge the OLD compiler and
 report that nothing changed.

  ce-kernel-doc : List Text = ["The compiler to judge. Empty means compile.ps1's own default, which is", "build-output/bare-metal/Codex.cdx and therefore whichever kernel ran", "LAST. Every caller inside a gate passes this explicitly."]

  ce-params : List ShellParam = [sh-doc ce-kernel-doc (sh-param-default "Kernel" SptString (SeLit "")), sh-param-default "Jobs" SptInt (SeInt 8)]

Section: The pipeline, declared before it is spelled

  tests-art : PipeArtifact = PipeArtifact { pa-name = "tests", pa-kind = PkValue, pa-expr = SeVar "tests", pa-from = None }

  out-root-art : PipeArtifact = PipeArtifact { pa-name = "outRoot", pa-kind = PkDir, pa-expr = SeVar "outRoot", pa-from = None }

  bad-art : PipeArtifact = PipeArtifact { pa-name = "bad", pa-kind = PkValue, pa-expr = SeVar "bad", pa-from = None }

  skipped-art : PipeArtifact = PipeArtifact { pa-name = "skipped", pa-kind = PkValue, pa-expr = SeVar "skipped", pa-from = None }

  passed-art : PipeArtifact = PipeArtifact { pa-name = "passed", pa-kind = PkValue, pa-expr = SeVar "passed", pa-from = None }

  ce-arts : List PipeArtifact = [tests-art, out-root-art, bad-art, skipped-art, passed-art]

Section: S01 -- Derive the set

  s01-body : List ShellCmd = [ScRaw "Set-StrictMode -Version Latest", ScRaw "$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'", ScRaw "Set-Location (Join-Path $PSScriptRoot '..')", ScRaw "[Environment]::CurrentDirectory = (Get-Location).Path", ScBlank, ScComment "176 tests assert a REFUSAL, and until 2026-08-17 the gate ran 13 of them.", ScComment "", ScComment "codex/test/errors is the diagnostic path: each source is a program the", ScComment "compiler must reject, and its .failing names the codes that must fire. The", ScComment "set is reachable only from build/test.ps1, which is the battery and refuses", ScComment "to run without Damian. bvt.ps1 carries thirteen by name. So a rejection that", ScComment "stopped happening, or started happening for a different reason, was caught", ScComment "by nothing an agent is allowed to run.", ScComment "", ScComment "That is not hypothetical. bounded-exceeded declared `bounded linear` over a", ScComment "loop appending a text LITERAL; COMPILER-8 made that extend in place, rule 3", ScComment "stopped inferring it growing, the declaration held, and the test compiled", ScComment "clean -- the exact opposite of what it exists to assert. It reached main", ScComment "green in Update 45 and was found by a release battery, not by a gate.", ScComment "", ScComment "The set is derived from the directory, never listed here. A hand-maintained", ScComment "list is how the thirteen came to stand for a hundred and seventy-six.", ScComment "", ScComment "Exit 1 on any test that compiles, that fails with the wrong codes, or that", ScComment "declares nothing at all.", ScBlank, ScRaw "$errDir = Join-Path 'codex' (Join-Path 'test' 'errors')", ScRaw "if (-not (Test-Path -PathType Container $errDir)) {", ScRaw "    Write-Host \"FAIL: $errDir is missing\"", ScRaw "    exit 1", ScRaw "}", ScBlank, ScRaw "$tests = @(Get-ChildItem $errDir -Filter *.codex -File | ForEach-Object { $_.FullName } | Sort-Object)", ScRaw "if ($tests.Count -eq 0) {", ScRaw "    Write-Host \"FAIL: no tests under $errDir -- a check over an empty set passes for free\"", ScRaw "    exit 1", ScRaw "}", ScBlank]

 THE EMPTY-SET REFUSAL IS THE ONE WORTH NAMING: a check over no subjects is
 green for free, so the absence of tests is itself a failure here (L-DENOM).

  s01 : PipeStage = PipeStage { ps-name = "derive the set", ps-why = "every refusal test is taken from the directory, never from a list, because a hand-maintained list is how thirteen came to stand for a hundred and seventy-six", ps-in = [], ps-out = [tests-art], ps-needs = [], ps-verdict = [PoExit 1 "codex/test/errors does not exist; spelled inside a raw payload", PoExit 1 "codex/test/errors holds no test at all, and a check over an empty set passes for free; spelled inside a raw payload"], ps-body = s01-body }

Section: S02 -- Compile each, in parallel

  s02-body : List ShellCmd = [ScRaw "$outRoot = Join-Path 'test-output' '_errors'", ScRaw "if (Test-Path $outRoot) { Remove-Item -Recurse -Force $outRoot }", ScRaw "New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path $outRoot | Out-Null", ScBlank, ScRaw "$sw = [System.Diagnostics.Stopwatch]::StartNew()", ScRaw "Write-Host \"  check-errors: $($tests.Count) refusals, $Jobs parallel slots\"", ScBlank, ScRaw "$compileScript = Join-Path (Resolve-Path .).Path 'build\\compile.ps1'", ScRaw "$bad = [System.Collections.Concurrent.ConcurrentBag[string]]::new()", ScRaw "$skipped = [System.Collections.Concurrent.ConcurrentBag[string]]::new()", ScRaw "$passed = [System.Collections.Concurrent.ConcurrentBag[string]]::new()", ScBlank, ScRaw "$tests | ForEach-Object -ThrottleLimit $Jobs -Parallel {", ScRaw "    $t = $_", ScRaw "    $base = [System.IO.Path]::GetFileNameWithoutExtension($t)", ScRaw "    $skipFile = $t -replace '\\.codex$', '.skip'", ScRaw "    if (Test-Path -PathType Leaf $skipFile) {", ScRaw "        ($using:skipped).Add(\"$base ($((Get-Content -TotalCount 1 $skipFile).Trim()))\")", ScRaw "        return", ScRaw "    }", ScRaw "    $failFile = $t -replace '\\.codex$', '.failing'", ScRaw "    if (-not (Test-Path -PathType Leaf $failFile)) {", ScRaw "        ($using:bad).Add(\"$base -- no .failing sidecar: the test asserts nothing\")", ScRaw "        return", ScRaw "    }", ScRaw "    $codes = @(Get-Content $failFile | ForEach-Object { $_.Trim() } | Where-Object { $_ })", ScRaw "    if ($codes.Count -eq 0) {", ScRaw "        ($using:bad).Add(\"$base -- .failing is empty: the test asserts nothing\")", ScRaw "        return", ScRaw "    }", ScRaw "    $outDir = Join-Path $using:outRoot $base", ScRaw "    New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path $outDir | Out-Null", ScRaw "    $cdxOut = Join-Path $outDir \"$base.cdx\"", ScRaw "    $logOut = Join-Path $outDir \"$base.log\"", ScRaw "    # NOT $args: that is an automatic variable, and assigning it inside a", ScRaw "    # scriptblock shadows the one splatting reads.", ScRaw "    $cargs = @('-Src', $t, '-Out', $cdxOut, '-Log', $logOut)", ScRaw "    if ($using:Kernel) { $cargs += @('-Kernel', $using:Kernel) }", ScRaw "    & pwsh -NoProfile -File $using:compileScript @cargs *> $null", ScRaw "    if ($LASTEXITCODE -eq 0) {", ScRaw "        ($using:bad).Add(\"$base -- COMPILED, and it must be refused ($($codes -join ' '))\")", ScRaw "        return", ScRaw "    }", ScRaw "    $logText = if (Test-Path $logOut) { Get-Content $logOut -Raw } else { '' }", ScRaw "    # test.ps1's adjudication, and it must stay identical to it: `error", ScRaw "    # (CDX)?0*<n>` rather than a bare CDX<n> search, because the lexer's codes", ScRaw "    # print unprefixed and single-digit (`error 6:`) and a CDX-prefixed search", ScRaw "    # reports those as wrong-code failures. A bare `CDX2031` checks only that", ScRaw "    # the code fired; `CDX2031@33:5` also pins WHERE, which a bare code cannot", ScRaw "    # -- a diagnostic reported at a synthetic 0,0 span prints no line:column", ScRaw "    # prefix at all, so a code-only check passes against a compiler that lost", ScRaw "    # the position entirely.", ScRaw "    $missing = ''", ScRaw "    foreach ($code in $codes) {", ScRaw "        if ($code -match '^(?<c>(CDX)?\\d+)@(?<l>\\d+):(?<col>\\d+)$') {", ScRaw "            $c = $matches['c'] -replace '^CDX', ''", ScRaw "            $pat = \"\\b$($matches['l']):$($matches['col']):\\s*error (CDX)?0*$c\\b\"", ScRaw "            if ($logText -notmatch $pat) { $missing = $code; break }", ScRaw "        } elseif ($logText -notmatch \"error (CDX)?0*$code\\b\") { $missing = $code; break }", ScRaw "    }", ScRaw "    if ($missing) {", ScRaw "        ($using:bad).Add(\"$base -- refused, but not with $missing (declared: $($codes -join ' '))\")", ScRaw "    } else {", ScRaw "        ($using:passed).Add($base)", ScRaw "    }", ScRaw "}", ScBlank]

 THIS STAGE IS THE ONLY ONE ON THE CAMPAIGN SO FAR THAT IS GENUINELY PARALLEL,
 and the guest count it declares is `-Jobs`' default rather than a fixed one.

  s02 : PipeStage = PipeStage { ps-name = "compile each, in parallel", ps-why = "every test must be REFUSED, and refused with the codes its .failing declares; a test that compiles is the defect this exists to catch", ps-in = ["tests", "Kernel", "Jobs"], ps-out = [out-root-art, bad-art, skipped-art, passed-art], ps-needs = [PrGuests 8], ps-verdict = [], ps-body = s02-body }

Section: S03 -- The verdict

  s03-body : List ShellCmd = [ScRaw "$sw.Stop()", ScRaw "$elapsed = [math]::Round($sw.Elapsed.TotalSeconds, 1)", ScBlank, ScRaw "if ($bad.Count -gt 0) {", ScRaw "    Write-Host ''", ScRaw "    Write-Host \"FAIL: $($bad.Count) of $($tests.Count) refusal test(s) did not refuse as declared:\"", ScRaw "    foreach ($b in ($bad | Sort-Object)) { Write-Host \"  $b\" }", ScRaw "    Write-Host ''", ScRaw "    Write-Host '  A test here asserts the compiler REFUSES a program, and what it refuses'", ScRaw "    Write-Host '  with is the assertion. A rejection that moved to a different code is a'", ScRaw "    Write-Host '  diagnostic regression; one that stopped happening is a soundness hole.'", ScRaw "    Write-Host \"  Per-test logs: $outRoot\\<name>\\<name>.log\"", ScRaw "    exit 1", ScRaw "}", ScBlank, ScRaw "$skipNote = if ($skipped.Count -gt 0) { \", $($skipped.Count) skipped\" } else { '' }", ScRaw "Write-Host \"  refusals ok ($($passed.Count) refused as declared$skipNote, ${elapsed}s)\"", ScRaw "foreach ($s in ($skipped | Sort-Object)) { Write-Host \"    skipped: $s\" }", ScRaw "exit 0"]

 A SKIPPED TEST IS NOT COUNTED AGAINST THE VERDICT: `$skipped` is reported and
 never reaches `$bad`, so a `.skip` beside a refusal test removes it from the
 assertion silently as far as the exit code is concerned.

  s03 : PipeStage = PipeStage { ps-name = "verdict", ps-why = "refuse if any test compiled, refused with the wrong code, or declared nothing", ps-in = ["bad", "skipped", "passed", "tests", "outRoot"], ps-out = [], ps-needs = [], ps-verdict = [PoExit 1 "at least one test compiled when it must be refused, refused with a code its .failing does not declare, or carries no assertion at all; spelled inside a raw payload", PoExit 0 "every test not skipped refused with the codes it declares; spelled inside a raw payload"], ps-body = s03-body }

Section: Assembly

  ce-pipe : Pipeline = Pipeline { pl-name = "check-errors", pl-doc = "every test under codex/test/errors must be REFUSED, with the codes it declares.", pl-params = ce-params, pl-stages = [s01, s02, s03] }

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (emit-powershell (pipeline-to-shell ce-pipe))
  end

